{"packet_id":"D027-01","doc_id":"D027","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California aggregate income screening standard","requirement":"A landlord may not use a financial or income standard in renting housing that fails to count the combined income of persons living together on the same basis as the combined income of married persons living together.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All housing accommodations offered for rent or lease in California; the text states no building-age, unit-count or owner-type limits.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-01-01","citation":"Cal. Gov. Code § 12955","quoted_span":"(n) To use a financial or income standard in the rental of housing that fails to account for the aggregate income of persons residing together or proposing to reside together on the same basis as the aggregate income of married persons residing together or proposing to reside together.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D027-01","doc_id":"D027","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California voucher-holder screening protections","requirement":"When a tenant has a government rent subsidy, a landlord must base any income eligibility standard on the tenant's share of the rent and may not use credit history without allowing verifiable alternative proof of ability to pay.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rentals where the tenant has a government rent subsidy; no building-age, unit-count or owner-type limits stated.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Does not limit the owner's ability to request employment information, landlord references, or to verify the identity of a person.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-01-01","citation":"Cal. Gov. Code § 12955","quoted_span":"(o) (1) In instances in which there is a government rent subsidy, to do either of the following: (A) Use a financial or income standard in assessing eligibility for the rental of housing that is not based on the portion of the rent to be paid by the tenant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D027-01","doc_id":"D027","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California source-of-income discrimination prohibition","requirement":"A landlord may not discriminate in the rental of housing because of a person's source of income, which includes lawful, verifiable income such as Section 8 housing vouchers paid on a tenant's behalf.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All housing accommodations in California; no building-age, unit-count or owner-type limits stated.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-01-01","citation":"Cal. Gov. Code § 12955","quoted_span":"(a) For the owner of any housing accommodation to discriminate against or harass any person because of the race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, marital status, national origin, ancestry, familial status, source of income, disability, veteran or military status, or genetic information of that person.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
